--[[
	SCRIPT DUMP EXPLORER  v3
	------------------------
	Scans the place for every Script / LocalScript / ModuleScript and saves the
	whole lot to a file on disk.

	HOW TO RUN
	  Studio > View > Command Bar, paste this whole file, press Enter.

	READ THIS ABOUT SAVING TO A FILE
	  Roblox Studio is sandboxed and has NO filesystem API. There is no
	  writefile() in Studio. So "Save to File" picks the best method available
	  in your environment, in this order:

	  1. writefile()   - only exists in exploit executors, not Studio. Used
	                     automatically if present. One .txt per script plus a
	                     combined dump.
	  2. HTTP POST     - set CONFIG.HttpEndpoint below and run the tiny local
	                     server (see the note at the bottom of this file). This
	                     is the only way to get a real automated file write out
	                     of Studio. Needs Game Settings > Security >
	                     "Allow HTTP Requests" turned on.
	  3. RBXMX EXPORT  - the fallback that always works. Builds the dump into
	                     ServerStorage.ScriptDump and selects it, so you can
	                     right-click the folder in Explorer > "Save to File..."
	                     and get a .rbxmx on disk. It's XML, so the source is
	                     plain readable text inside it.
]]

